[38;2;124;124;124mSymmetry gives P_n(y, x+2) = P_n(x+2, y) and P_n(y, x) = P_n(x, y). Then (***) [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mgives (x+1) P_n(x+2, y) = (y+1) P_n(x, y+2) + (x-y) P_n(x, y).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mP_{n+1}(y,x) = (x+y-1)(x+1) P_n(x+2, y) + x(1-x) P_n(x, y)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= (x+y-1)[(y+1) P_n(x, y+2) + (x-y) P_n(x, y)] + x(1-x) P_n(x, y)  [using (***)][0m[38;2;124;124;124m= (x+y-1)(y+1) P_n(x, y+2) + (x+y-1)(x-y) P_n(x, y) + x(1-x) P_n(x, y)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= (x+y-1)(y+1) P_n(x, y+2) + [(x+y-1)(x-y) + x(1-x)] P_n(x, y)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mNow (x+y-1)(x-y) + x(1-x) = x² - y² - x + y + x - x² = -y² + y = y(1-y).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo P_{n+1}(y,x) = (x+y-1)(y+1) P_n(x, y+2) + y(1-y) P_n(x, y) = P_{n+1}(x, y). ✓[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mGreat, so the proof is clean. Let me write it up.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe structure:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m1. Define the key identity (***): (y+1) P_n(x, y+2) + (x-y) P_n(x, y) = (x+1) [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mP_n(x+2, y)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2. Prove by induction that for all n: (a) P_n is symmetric, (b) P_n satisfies [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m(***).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m3. Base case n=1: both are trivially true.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m4. Inductive step: [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m   - (a) follows from (b) of P_n and (a) of P_n.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m   - (b) follows from (b) of P_n alone (algebraic verification).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write the clean proof now.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me also verify the key algebraic identity in step 2 more [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcarefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe need: (x-y)(x+y-1) - (y+1)(y+2) = (x+y+1)(x-y-2) + y(1-y)[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLHS = (x-y)(x+y-1) - (y+1)(y+2)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= (x² + xy - x - xy - y² + y) - (y² + 3y + 2)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= x² - x - y² + y - y² - 3y - 2[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= x² - x - 2y² - 2y - 2[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mRHS = (x+y+1)(x-y-2) + y(1-y)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= (x² - xy - 2x + xy - y² - 2y + x - y - 2) + y - y²[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= x² - x - y² - 3y - 2 + y - y²[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m= x² - x - 2y² - 2y - 2[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLHS = RHS ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mGreat. Now let me also verify the third terms match:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mLHS third term: (x-y)y(1-y) P_n(x,y)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mRHS third term: y(1-y)(x-y) P_n(x,y)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mThese are obviously equal. ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mAnd first terms:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mLHS: (y+1)(x+y+1)(y+3) P_n(x, y+4)[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mRHS: (x+y+1)(y+1)(y+3) P_n(x, y+4)[0m
